1
00:00:03,819 --> 00:00:07,539
Chapter 14.

2
00:00:09,158 --> 00:00:12,158
The fifth planet was very strange.

3
00:00:12,158 --> 00:00:14,560
It was the smallest of all.

4
00:00:14,560 --> 00:00:19,840
There was just enough room on it for a street lamp and a lamplighter.

5
00:00:19,840 --> 00:00:23,738
The little prince was not able to reach any explanation of the use of a street

6
00:00:23,738 --> 00:00:27,819
lamp and a lamplighter, somewhere in the heavens, on a planet, which was so small

7
00:00:27,819 --> 00:00:31,719
that it had no people, and not one house.

8
00:00:31,719 --> 00:00:35,880
But he said to himself, nevertheless

9
00:00:36,520 --> 00:00:41,560
he well be that this man is absurd. But he's not so absurd as the king, the

10
00:00:41,560 --> 00:00:46,359
conceited man, the businessman or the tipler For at least his work has some

11
00:00:46,359 --> 00:00:51,520
meaning. When he lights his street lamp, it is if he brought one more star to

12
00:00:51,520 --> 00:00:57,279
life for one flower. When he puts out his lamp, he sends the flower, or the star, to

13
00:00:57,279 --> 00:00:58,600
sleep.

14
00:00:58,600 --> 00:01:01,179
That is a beautiful occupation.

15
00:01:01,179 --> 00:01:07,000
And since it is beautiful, it is truly useful."

16
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:13,300
When he arrived on the planet he respectfully saluted the lamplighter.

17
00:01:13,300 --> 00:01:18,840
"Good morning sir Why have you just put out your lamp?"

18
00:01:19,960 --> 00:01:24,460
"Those are the orders," replied the lamplighter.

19
00:01:24,460 --> 00:01:27,119
"Good morning."

20
00:01:27,219 --> 00:01:30,359
"What are the orders?"

21
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:34,179
"The orders that I put out my lamp.

22
00:01:34,179 --> 00:01:36,219
Good evening."

23
00:01:36,219 --> 00:01:39,840
And he lighted his lamp again

24
00:01:40,539 --> 00:01:43,600
why have you just lighted it again?"

25
00:01:43,600 --> 00:01:48,039
"Those are the orders," replied the lamplighter.

26
00:01:48,039 --> 00:01:52,719
"I do not understand the little prince.

27
00:01:52,719 --> 00:01:56,979
"There is nothing to understand," said the lamplighter.

28
00:01:56,979 --> 00:01:59,260
"Orders or orders.

29
00:01:59,260 --> 00:02:01,359
Good morning."

30
00:02:01,359 --> 00:02:03,819
And he put out his lamp.

31
00:02:03,819 --> 00:02:09,698
Then he mopped his forehead with a handkerchief decorated with red squares

32
00:02:09,698 --> 00:02:12,640
when we follow a terrible profession.

33
00:02:12,640 --> 00:02:17,920
In the old days it was reasonable when I put the lamp out in the morning,

34
00:02:17,920 --> 00:02:22,179
and in the evening I lighted it again all right the rest of the day for

35
00:02:22,179 --> 00:02:26,319
relaxation and the rest of the night for sleep."

36
00:02:26,319 --> 00:02:30,100
"And the orders have been changed since that time?"

37
00:02:30,100 --> 00:02:36,880
"The orders have not been changed," said the lamplighter. "That is the tragedy!

38
00:02:36,880 --> 00:02:43,539
From year to year the planet has turned more rapidly and the orders have not been changed!"

39
00:02:43,539 --> 00:02:45,039
"Then what?"

40
00:02:45,039 --> 00:02:47,198
asked the little prince.

41
00:02:47,198 --> 00:02:52,000
"Then-- the planet now makes a complete turn every minute,

42
00:02:52,000 --> 00:02:56,020
and I no longer have a single second for repose.

43
00:02:56,020 --> 00:03:01,000
Once every minute I have to light my lamp and put it out!"

44
00:03:01,000 --> 00:03:03,219
"That is very funny!

45
00:03:03,219 --> 00:03:06,399
A day lasts only one minute, here where you live!"

46
00:03:06,399 --> 00:03:11,800
"It is not funny at all set the lamplighter. "While we've been talking

47
00:03:11,800 --> 00:03:16,840
together a month has gone by month?"

48
00:03:16,840 --> 00:03:22,600
"Yes, a month 30 minutes 30 days.

49
00:03:22,600 --> 00:03:28,380
Good evening when he lighted his lamp again.

50
00:03:29,920 --> 00:03:34,600
As the little prince watched him, he felt that he loved this lamplighter

51
00:03:34,600 --> 00:03:36,939
who was so faithful to his orders.

52
00:03:36,939 --> 00:03:40,600
He remembered the sunsets, which he himself had gone to seek, in other days,

53
00:03:40,600 --> 00:03:47,100
merely by pulling up his chair; and he wanted to help his friend.

54
00:03:47,140 --> 00:03:54,100
"You know," he said, "I can tell you a way you can rest whenever you want to..."

55
00:03:54,100 --> 00:04:00,460
"I always want to rest," said the lamplighter but it is possible for a man to be

56
00:04:00,460 --> 00:04:05,198
faithful and lazy at the same time.

57
00:04:05,198 --> 00:04:12,698
The little prince went on with his explanation: "Your planet is so small that three

58
00:04:12,698 --> 00:04:17,020
strides will take you all the way around it. To be always in the sunshine, you need

59
00:04:17,020 --> 00:04:19,779
only walk along rather slowly.

60
00:04:19,779 --> 00:04:27,060
When you want to rest, you will walk-- and the day will last as long as you like

61
00:04:27,158 --> 00:04:31,840
well That doesn't do me much good," said the lamplighter.

62
00:04:31,840 --> 00:04:39,760
"The one thing I love in life is to sleep oh Then you are unlucky,"

63
00:04:39,760 --> 00:04:42,279
said the little prince.

64
00:04:42,279 --> 00:04:47,619
"I am unlucky," said the lamplighter.

65
00:04:47,619 --> 00:04:50,460
"Good morning."

66
00:04:50,560 --> 00:04:54,060
And he put out his lamp.

67
00:04:55,840 --> 00:05:02,439
"That man," said the little prince to himself, as he continued father on his journey,

68
00:05:02,439 --> 00:05:07,420
"that man would be scorned by all the others: by the king, by the conceited man,

69
00:05:07,420 --> 00:05:10,119
by the tipler by the businessman.

70
00:05:10,119 --> 00:05:16,179
Nevertheless he's the only one of them all who does not seem to me ridiculous.

71
00:05:16,179 --> 00:05:21,779
Perhaps that is because he is thinking of something else besides himself."

72
00:05:21,939 --> 00:05:27,179
He breathed the sigh of regret, and said to himself, again

73
00:05:28,960 --> 00:05:33,880
man is the only one of them all whom I could have made my friend

74
00:05:33,880 --> 00:05:36,880
it is indeed too small.

75
00:05:36,880 --> 00:05:41,279
There is no room on it for two people..."

76
00:05:42,039 --> 00:05:48,340
What the little prince did not dare confess was that he was sorry most of all to

77
00:05:48,340 --> 00:06:00,819
leave this planet, because it was blessed every day with 1 4040 sunsets
